notes: "Before the last slide, the people and projects this work stands on. Three of them are in the code. OpenSlide is the foundation: the editor, canvas, Inspector, presentation and export come from it. Three equation-conversion modules come from OpenPPTD, and PptxGenJS writes the PowerPoint files. Everything else is a relationship of ideas, not code. I first met the PPTD idea in the Kimi Slides ecosystem, and the community open-kimi-ppt-skill notes helped with the format. PowerPoint, WPS and VS Code shaped the workspace: sections, notes, views, tabs and panels. OpenSlides Studio and the OpenPresentation format shaped how objects get stable IDs and how changes are checked against a revision. And I studied PPTist, Slidev, Presenton, PPTAgent and PPT Master as alternatives; each solves part of this problem well, and each taught me something specific. None of them endorses HUANDENG. The full list, with links and what was adopted, is in docs/ACKNOWLEDGMENTS.md in the repository.\n\nReference URLs (names link to source repositories or official sites):\nHUANDENG: https://github.com/JaytonKogeru/huandeng\nOpenSlide: https://github.com/open-slide/open-slide\nOpenPPTD: https://github.com/Shingwha/open-pptd\nPptxGenJS: https://github.com/gitbrent/PptxGenJS\nPowerPoint: https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/powerpoint\nWPS: https://www.wps.com/\nKimi / Moonshot AI: https://www.kimi.com/\nopen-kimi-ppt-skill: https://github.com/Amonginin/open-kimi-ppt-skill\nPPTist: https://github.com/pipipi-pikachu/PPTist\nVS Code: https://github.com/microsoft/vscode\nSlidev: https://github.com/slidevjs/slidev\nPresenton: https://github.com/presenton/presenton\nPPTAgent: https://github.com/icip-cas/PPTAgent\nPPTMaster: https://github.com/hugohe3/ppt-master\nOpenSlides Studio: https://gitlab.com/open-slides/openslides\nOPF: https://github.com/OpenPresentation/opf\nApache ECharts: https://github.com/apache/echarts\nKaTeX: https://github.com/KaTeX/KaTeX\nFont Awesome: https://github.com/FortAwesome/Font-Awesome\nOpenSlides Studio website: https://openslides.dev/\nOPF website: https://www.openpresentation.org/\n"
